RF.put("questb:b28",{"8668":{"id":8668,"t":"Genesis Trousers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Skin of the Great Sandworm, 2 Idols of War, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nSkin of the Great Sandworm Ouro\n2 Idol of War Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"You seek to prove your worth to my kind, mortal? Very well, perhaps we can be of mutual assistance.\nThe ancient sandworm, Ouro, is a being of legendary power. He is rumored to have been created by the Old God himself as a mockery of life.\nHis skin is unnatural... thick, nearly impregnable, yet it's flexible and allows him to move with the speed and grace of a much smaller creature.\nBring me a sample of his skin along with other minor components and I shall craft you leggings of great power.","rew":"You will receive:\nGenesis Trousers\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Did you bring the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"Yes... the worm's skin will make for an excellent protective layer. Combined with the strongest parts from the Qiraji we've destroyed on our way here, this should make for a formidable piece of armor. May it aid you in facing the unspeakable horrors that await inside!\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Druid Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8668\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Genesis Trousers this quest\nBring the Skin of the Great Sandworm, 2 Idols of War, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8588":{"id":8588,"t":"The Horde Needs Heavy Leather!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 53.","obj":"Bring 10 Heavy Leather to Skinner Jamani at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n10 Heavy Leather Advanced Target Dummy 90 % , Felsteel Chest 3.6 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 2.5 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 2.5 % and 4 more","desc":"Since we're preparing for war, it might be best if we get all of the goods we need first, don't you think, mon? One of the staples of the war materiel that we're producing is heavy leather. We'll use it for just about everything, from reinforcement to armor, and good old plain tarps too.\nBut first we need to get our hands on more of it. That's your job, ‹class›. Sharpen your knife and bring me back a bundle. Then we'll talk further.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"I've got no time for games if you're just here to jibber-jabber, ‹class›. There are too many stacks of heavy leather that need curing. Come back when you have at least ten for me.","done":"Simply amazing... look at the purity of these samples. Hmm, I wonder what it could mean. They seem to be elemental in nature, but... something more. They remind me of... of the Old Gods. We've found traces of them throughout Azeroth, and now I wonder if these creatures aren't related to them somehow.\nWe shall have to test further.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.6,"y":73.3,"n":"Skinner Jamani","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"668":{"id":668,"t":"Sunken Treasure","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Elven Gems to Captain O'Breen.\nElven Gems\nProvided: Elven Gems","desc":"Let's not leave Captain O'Breen waiting. He'll want to see these gems first hand. After all, that's why we're here!\nAnd after a few weeks of consorting with these pirates, the professor and I have realized the last thing that's good for our health is to be caught hanging on to their treasure.\nHere, ‹name›, take these to O'Breen.","rew":"Experience: 1,550\n+50 reputation with Booty Bay\n-250 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Ahoy, ‹class›. What brings you to the bridge?","done":"So the little gnomes proved their worth after all? I knew we kept those ankle biters around for a reason!","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":33.9,"y":80.4,"n":"Doctor Draxlegauge","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":32.3,"y":81.4,"n":"Shakes O'Breen","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"908":{"id":908,"t":"Amongst the ruins","lv":27,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Fathom Core to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.\nFathom Core","desc":"The Twilight's Hammer has moved into the Moonshrine Ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. Their presence can only serve to coerce the elements into working against us. If left unchecked, this region will be theirs for good.\n‹name›, go into Blackfathom and find the ruin's fathom stone; it should be somewhere close in the water. In it is a fathom core - a device that when properly read it will relate a history of all elemental activity. If I have it, I and the Earthen Ring can maybe do something to stop them!","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\nLevel 27 , requires level 25 Difficulty 25 30 35 Side Both factions Type Elite Shareable Yes Quest ID 908","cats":["ashenvale"]},"7868":{"id":7868,"t":"Outrider Advanced Care Package","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nOutrider Advanced Care Package\nExperience: 650\n+10 reputation with Warsong Outriders","done":"You've certainly begun to prove yourself to us, ‹name›. As a reward, please take this care package! Inside it you'll find rations and bandages that are usable only inside Warsong Gulch.\nAs you continue to prove yourself inside the Gulch, you'll find that these items will become available to you for purchase. Rations become available when you are Friendly with us, and bandages when you are Honored.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.4,"n":"Kelm Hargunth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"8988":{"id":8988,"t":"More Components of Importance","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Obtain Soul Ashes of the Banished and return them to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\nSoul Ashes of the Banished Writhing Mage , Cursed Justicar , Cursed Paladin","desc":"‹class›, listen closely. Now that we have the location of the last amulet piece, we still need another component to suffuse the brazier with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to entice the spirit of my deceased, former comrade.\nAn ogre necromancer that traveled with us, Kormok, delighted in summoning forth the souls of the banished dead of Purgation Isle, off the south coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Go there and retrieve some Soul Ashes of the Banished from their remains.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n3 Bloodkelp Elixir of Dodging 3 Bloodkelp Elixir of Resistance\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you returned already then, ‹class›, with what I sent you out to gather?","done":"A job well done, ‹name›. I will imbue the essence of the ashes into the brazier.\nNow all that is left is to get into Scholomance, to Ras Frostwhisper's chamber, and use the brazier to summon forth the spirit of my former cohort, Kormok. The amulet piece, and Valthalak's spirit within, has corrupted him even further, and he will not rest until you forcibly take it from him.\nOh, by the way, I had some leftover bloodkelp from your trip to Alcaz Isle, so I made it into some potions for you. Take your pick!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"3628":{"id":3628,"t":"You Are Rakh'likh, Demon","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy Razelikh the Defiler and return the Severed Horn of the Defiler to the Fallen Hero of the Horde. You will also need to return the Ward of the Defiler so that the Fallen Hero can destroy it, preventing it from ever falling into the wrong hands.\nSevered Horn of the Defiler Razelikh the Defiler\nWard of the Defiler\nProvided: Ward of the Defiler","desc":"Razelikh's lair is atop the highest mountain in the Blasted Lands. The only way to the lair is through the use of the teleport runes near the mountain. As long as you hold the amulet, you can freely transport up to the lair. Once you reach the lair, you must conjure the beast. The amulet is your key, ‹name›. Use it on the Altar of the Defiler.\nShould you defeat the Defiler, bring back his horn. It will become a symbol of hope for all that view it - proof that heroes do exist in this war torn world.","rew":"You will receive:\nNecklace of Sanctuary Demon's Blood Demon Hide Sack\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950","back":"There is nothing left to fear.","done":"Today is a day that will be remembered for all eternity. The demonic overlord of the Blasted Lands has finally fallen!\nSwamp of Sorrows Blasted Lands","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"97948":{"id":97948,"t":"Camping 101 mining","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Kurdram Stonehammer in Auberdine to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your mining skill to 20","desc":"Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Lodestone. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nTeldrassil Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":38.2,"y":41,"n":"Kurdram Stonehammer","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96988":{"id":96988,"t":"Source of power","lv":33,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 6 Cracked Sentry Cores in the City of Dalaran for Doctor Martin Felben in Undercity.\n6 Cracked Sentry Core","desc":"With the city of Dalaran under siege by their own constructs, this is the perfect opportunity to, let's say, borrow a few samples.\nImagine an army of arcane-powered abominations. The Dark Lady would have no choice but to recognize my alchemical prowess. Maybe even grant me head of the Royal Apothecary Society?\nGo to the city and find the constructs' cores. They are unlikely to give them willingly, so do what you must.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nUnstable Power Core Construct Cloak\nExperience: 9,400","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":46.6,"y":74.4,"n":"Doctor Martin Felben","s":1}],"cats":["city-of-dalaran"]},"94348":{"id":94348,"t":"Craftsmans writ chimeric vest","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Chimeric Vest\nChimeric Vest","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Chimeric Vest, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Chimeric Vest Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94348","cats":["crafting"]},"94268":{"id":94268,"t":"Craftsmans writ steel plate helm","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Steel Plate Helm\nSteel Plate Helm","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Steel Plate Helm, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Steel Plate Helm Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94268","cats":["crafting"]},"98028":{"id":98028,"t":"Baron marinous","lv":21,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Clouded Water Globe to Onu at the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore.\nProvided: Clouded Water Globe","desc":"All that remains of the powerful elemental is a globe of what seems to be pure water, clouded by some unknown substance. The edges of the sphere seem to be clear until you turn it--as if the cloud actively prevents you from peering within.\nWhatever happened to it--and to the ruins it was guarding--is still active in some way.\nOnly Onu, the Ancient of Lore at the Grove of the Ancients to the far south, would have a chance at knowing more.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMathystra Channeling Orb Onu's Patience\nMoney: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,050\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"I can sense something far older than you in my presence, ‹race›... what have you brought me?","done":"<Onu appears surprised--or as surprised as an ancient can appear.>\nStairs descending down in Mathystra? Could be it be?\n<Onu shakes his head.>\nI must confer with the others on this. For now, know that it is good you uncovered this before the naga... or their cult allies.\nPlease accept this as thanks for your efforts. It is no small feat to defeat an elemental guardian.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":43.6,"y":76.4,"n":"Onu","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"28":{"id":28,"t":"Trial of the Lake","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find a Shrine Bauble in Lake Elune'ara, and take it to the Shrine of Remulos in northwestern Moonglade. Once there, use the Shrine Bauble.\nYou must speak with Tajarri at the shrine afterwards in order to complete the trial.","desc":"For your first trial, search the depths of Lake Elune'ara to locate a Shrine Bauble. It decays rapidly, so proceed with it to the Shrine of Remulos post haste. Use the bauble at the shrine, and then speak with Tajarri there; she is one of Moonglade's most trusted wardens.\nYou only have a set amount of time to complete the task, and you may be competing against other druids searching for baubles themselves. Mental and physical dexterity will be critical to your success.\nGood luck, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 875\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Well now. It looks like yet another ‹race› has successfully completed the Trial of the Lake! Well done, my young friend - well done.\nAs I've said, my name is Tajarri. It is my duty and my privilege to serve as a warden for Moonglade, and specifically this shrine. Keeper Remulos guides the Cenarion Circle in preservation of nature and balance, and his shrine serves as a lasting tribute to such. By using the bauble here, it serves as a nod to the importance of this place within the Circle.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":36.5,"y":40.1,"n":"Tajarri","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"828":{"id":828,"t":"Margoz","lv":12,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Margoz.","desc":"One of our Shamans, Margoz, knows more of the Burning Blade's corruption. He speaks of a cave called Skull Rock in the mountains - just outside Orgrimmar! - that shelters a large band of Burning Blade cultists.\nBefore you go to Skull Rock speak with Margoz. He is wise and his council is valued.\nHe is camped to the northeast, between the coast and Drygulch Ravine.\nFollow his advice, but whatever Margoz says, ‹name›, I still want you to crush those cultists!","rew":"Experience: 90\n+10 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+10 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","done":"Welcome, ‹name›. Word reached me of your coming, and of your exploits in Durotar.\nYou are a ‹class› of growing skill and renown.\nStay on the pure path, and your future will be great indeed.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52.2,"y":43.2,"n":"Orgnil Soulscar","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":56.4,"y":20,"n":"Margoz","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"268":{"id":268,"t":"Return to Sven","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Sven with Jitters' completed journal.\nJitters' Completed Journal\nProvided: Jitters' Completed Journal","desc":"The book you found was only half finished. I had to leave it at Sven's farm when I fled there...\nHere. Take my completed journal to Sven. It describes more fully what happened at his farm.\nAlthough this journal has been my only company these past weeks, if giving it up keeps me from having to face Sven and his wrath, then I do it willingly!","rew":"Experience: 500\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you find who the Shadowy Figure was?","done":"This journal explains much to me, and sets me on the path against the dark riders! I have seen these riders in Duskwood, and have seen them speak with the wizard Morbent Fel, at the Forlorn Rowe.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":18.4,"y":56.4,"n":"Jitters","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":7.8,"y":34.1,"n":"Sven Yorgen","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1388":{"id":1388,"t":"Nothing But The Truth","lv":42,"min":37,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Faustin's Truth Serum to Deathstalker Zraedus at Beggar's Haunt.\nFaustin's Truth Serum\nProvided: Faustin's Truth Serum","desc":"Everything is proceeding according to plan, ‹name›. I want you to give this truth serum to Deathstalker Zraedus and he'll show you how to administer it.... properly.\nHaha!","rew":"Experience: 350\n+25 reputation with Undercity","back":"I hope you have proven yourself of use to our dear friend, Apothecary Faustin.","done":"I knew old Faustin would come up with something good! You were a tremendous help, no doubt.\nNow let's get down to business, shall we?","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":87.5,"y":35.2,"n":"Apothecary Faustin","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":87.8,"y":35.6,"n":"Deathstalker Zraedus","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"9228":{"id":9228,"t":"Epic Armaments of Battle - Exalted Amongst the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"For 27 Insignias of the Dawn and 27 Insignias of the Crusade you may choose an item from the Argent Dawn's treasure cache.\n27 Insignia of the Dawn\n27 Insignia of the Crusade","desc":"Greetings, friend. Have you insignias of the Dawn or the Crusade that you would like to redeem for items of great power?\nThose exalted amongst the Dawn receive our greatest discounts! I encourage you to make a purchase.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAmulet of the Dawn Bracers of Hope Bracers of Subterfuge Medallion of the Dawn Talisman of Ascendance The Purifier\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Choose carefully. There are no refunds.","done":"Good day, ‹name›. It was a pleasure doing business with you.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.8,"y":50.2,"n":"Quartermaster Miranda Breechlock","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"4108":{"id":4108,"t":"Salve via Hunting","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"6 Corrupted Soul Shard Ulathek 35 % , Xavaric 35 % , Prince Xavalis 35 % , Jaedenar Legionnaire 35 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve","back":"Possessing a Cenarion Beacon allows one to see a corrupted soul shard on those tainted beasts that are put down for the greater good. I grind shards into a usable reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. We will use that salve to turn corrupted plants into healthy ones again.\nIn exchange for these shards, I will give you some Cenarion plant salves I have already prepared.","done":"Very well then, here are your Cenarion plant salves. Scour Felwood for corrupted plants, ‹name›! Wherever they are, use the salve I have given you to purify them.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":46.7,"y":83.1,"n":"Maybess Riverbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"3788":{"id":3788,"t":"Jonespyre's Request","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Quintis Jonespyre in Feathermoon Stronghold.","desc":"Excuse me, friend...\nA colleague of mine would like to speak with you about the research you are doing in conjunction with the Cenarion Circle. He is a druid by the name of Quintis Jonespyre, and he resides here in Feathermoon Stronghold. He would like to confer with you about morrowgrain... and he very much would like for you to keep our discussion from the ears of the Arch Druid.\nIf you're interested, speak with him; no doubt, all will be revealed once you do.","rew":"Experience: 470\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","done":"I thank you for coming, weary traveler! Allow me to introduce myself - I am Quintis Jonespyre, druid and humble servant of Malfurion and the Cenarion Circle. My colleagues (General Shandris Feathermoon and the Protectorate - mayhap you've heard of us) and I wanted to talk with you about the work you are doing for Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.\nBefore we get much further, I'd like to ask that our discussion stay between just us. If you have no problem with this, then we may proceed.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":31,"y":43.5,"n":"Innkeeper Shyria","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":32.4,"y":43.8,"n":"Quintis Jonespyre","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"508":{"id":508,"t":"Taretha's Gift","lv":40,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return Taretha's pendant to Krusk in Tarren Mill.\nTaretha's Necklace\nProvided: Taretha's Necklace","desc":"The pendant? Of course you can have it... Take it! I want no memory of him... just please, please leave in peace...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMantis Boots Brigand's Pauldrons\nExperience: 3,900\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You've returned, ‹name›. Success to report?","done":"It is strange that the Warchief would expend so much over such a small thing. I do not claim to understand him, but I will follow him, whatever his commands. You did well, ‹name›, no doubt the Warchief will be glad to hear of your success.\nAlterac Mountains Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":39.3,"y":14.3,"n":"Elysa","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":63.2,"y":20.7,"n":"Krusk","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"8908":{"id":8908,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Lightforge Bracers to Deliana in Ironforge.\n15 Winterspring Blood Sample Rabid Shardtooth 30 % , Elder Shardtooth 30 % , Shardtooth Bear 30 % , Shardtooth Mauler 30 % and 4 more\nLightforge Bracers Lord Alexei Barov 5 % in Scholomance , Risen Protector 3.7 % in Scholomance , Risen Warrior 3.6 % in Scholomance , Rockwing Screecher 0.7 % and 1 more","desc":"Well met, ‹class›. I've something that might interest you.\nI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality. I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.\nThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment. Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold. You shall find the effort worth your while.","rew":"You will receive:\nSoulforge Bracers\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you brought me what I requested of you, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent! Let's perform the trade then. It's hard to part with this excellent armor, but I'm afraid I won't be needing it any time soon.\nIf you're interested in performing more work for me, I might be willing to give up the rest of the pieces.\nDun Morogh Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"5148":{"id":5148,"t":"Tribal Leatherworking","lv":55,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Wild Leather Vest and a Wild Leather Helmet to Se'Jib in Stranglethorn Vale.\nCompleting this quest will give you access to the Tribal Leatherworking arts.\nThe completion of this quest will prevent you from learning Dragonscale Leatherworking and Elemental Leatherworking; be sure this is the path you wish to follow before doing so.\nWild Leather Vest\nWild Leather Helmet","desc":"To learn tribal leatherworking demands an understanding of how primal nature truly is; I know that you have already mastered the art of making wild leather armor, and I am willing to complete your training.\nKnow this, ‹class›: by choosing this path you agree never to learn dragonscale or elemental leatherworking; there is only room for practice of one of the three arts. Furthermore, bring to me the finest samples of your wild leather armor. From there, we will begin your mastery.","rew":"You will learn: Tribal Leatherworking\nExperience: 4,200\n+200 reputation with Leatherworking - Tribal","back":"Nature is a force that must be appeased before you hope to learn how to bend its will into your leather garments. Bring me your offering to this force, and I will make sure you are heard.","done":"You've given your finest offerings, and nature will soon permit you to bend her to your will. Once I have finished my tutelage, your work will be a force of nature unto itself.\nTo train in the art for the future, simply speak to me and I will make available any knowledge that you have yet to commit as yours.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":36.5,"y":34.1,"n":"Se'Jib","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"1948":{"id":1948,"t":"Items of Power","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Jade and the Bolt Charged Bramble to Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.\nJade Accursed Slitherblade 2.7 % , Drulzegar Skraghook 2.1 % , Ruul Onestone 1.7 % , Ironeye the Invincible 1.6 % and 4 more\nBolt Charged Bramble Bolt Charged Bramble\nProvided: Tabetha's Instructions","desc":"The building of a mage's wand is not easy. Rare substances are required, and a vessel must be made that can store great quantities of magical energy. You must gather these things and bring them to me.\nI have written onto this parchment that which you need, and instructions on how to get it. Bring me exactly what is on this list, and follow my written directions to the letter, for if you do not then when we make your wand things might go... badly.","rew":"Experience: 3,150","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Do you have the items I require?","done":"Aha! You got the jade and made the bramble! Well done!\nIs that smoke I see rising from your ears? You might have gotten too close when the lightning struck the totem sticks, but don't worry. Being hit by lightning is good luck!\nDustwallow Marsh Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"7068":{"id":7068,"t":"Shadowshard Fragments","lv":42,"min":39,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 39 instead of 38.","obj":"Collect 10 Shadowshard Fragments from Maraudon and return them to Uthel'nay in Orgrimmar.\n10 Shadowshard Fragment Shadowshard Rumbler 80 % , Shadowshard Smasher 80 %","desc":"Strong magics be found in the centaur holy place... the holy place of Maraudon. The Desolace tribes of centaur protect that place wit' their lives, but they canna stop us from takin' what we need.\nYou, you head to this Maraudon place and find the rock creatures made of shadowshard. You bring me the purple crystals, and Uthel'nay make you somethin' for your time.\nThe place be dangerous, so maybe you be bringing some friends.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nZealous Shadowshard Pendant Prodigious Shadowshard Pendant\nExperience: 3,450\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"You find the crystals yet? Rituals of power, spells of great strength - those shadowshards maybe very helpful in all kind of arcane magics.","done":"Ah, these be perfect for me magics. Here, you take one of these trinkets and be on your way... me got much studyin' to do.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":39.2,"y":86.3,"n":"Uthel'nay","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["maraudon"]},"9388":{"id":9388,"t":"Flickering Flames in Kalimdor","lv":25,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 1,500 experience instead of 15,000, 0.1 times as much.","obj":"Visit the bonfires within Ashenvale, the Barrens, Darkshore, and Stonetalon Mountains, then speak with the Festival Flamekeeper.\nFlame of Ashenvale used\nFlame of the Barrens used\nFlame of Darkshore used\nFlame of Stonetalon used","desc":"There are many flames burning throughout the world today, ‹name›. The trickiest fires to tend are those that burn green; they do not stay lit long without supervision. Make certain the emerald fires still burn on Kalimdor for our Flamekeeper, eh?\nYou will find them near Ratchet in the Barrens, close to the Master's Glaive in Darkshore, in the forest of Ashenvale by the bridge near Silverwing Outpost, and near the road to Windshear Crag along the main road in Stonetalon Mountains.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Elderberry Pie 4 Fire-toasted Bun 5 Midsummer Sausage 5 Toasted Smorc\nExperience: 1,500","back":"The fires cannot die until the festival is done!","done":"Ahhh, so they do still burn. I am glad; it would not do for those fires to burn out before their time. You have done well, ‹name›. Take this with my blessing.\nTeldrassil Dun Morogh Stormwind City Thunder Bluff Orgrimmar Tirisfal Glades Ashenvale The Barrens Darkshore Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.5,"y":92.2,"n":"Festival Loremaster","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.6,"y":91.9,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.3,"y":25.1,"n":"Festival Loremaster","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50,"y":72,"n":"Festival Loremaster","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":21.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Festival Talespinner","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.8,"y":34.9,"n":"Festival Talespinner","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.6,"y":34.2,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.9,"y":73.1,"n":"Festival Talespinner","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"748":{"id":748,"t":"Poison Water","lv":5,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Prairie Wolf Paws and 4 Plainstrider Talons to Mull Thunderhorn in Bloodhoof.\n6 Prairie Wolf Paw Prairie Wolf 40 % , Prairie Wolf Alpha 15 % , Prairie Stalker 15 %\n4 Plainstrider Talon Mazzranache 50 % , Adult Plainstrider 50 % , Elder Plainstrider 50 % , Greater Plainstrider 50 % and 3 more","desc":"Goblins and their servants have tainted our sacred water wells! We cannot allow this.\nTo cleanse each well, I must create a cleansing totem, then you must bring the totem to the well and perform a cleansing ritual.\nFirst we will create a cleansing totem for the Winterhoof Water Well. To do this, the land must offer its aid. Hunt prairie wolves for their paws and adult plainstriders for their talons. They are to the southwest.\nReturn to me with the paws and talons, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 450\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Do you have the paws and talons, ‹name›?","done":"You have done well, ‹name›. I will take these and bind their power into a totem of cleansing.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.5,"y":63.6,"n":"Mull Thunderhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9068":{"id":9068,"t":"Earthshatter Tunic","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rimblat Earthshatter at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make an Earthshatter Tunic if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Tunic, 25 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 4 Arcanite Bars and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Tunic\n25 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Arcanite Bar\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"Would you honor me by returning the armor of those that fell in the defense of these lands?\nThe armor has been desecrated and is undoubtedly being used for evil; however, with wartorn armor scraps, the desecrated armor can be renewed and worn for battle once more.\nBring me the remnants of the fallen along with purification materials and Earthshatter shall be yours to don.\nSearch Naxxramas.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarthshatter Tunic\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Earthshatter Tunic.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.3,"y":49.4,"n":"Rimblat Earthshatter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1788":{"id":1788,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":13,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.","desc":"I'll take the script to the King's advisors after Duthorian's taken a look at them, but in the meantime, you should go speak to Duthorian now. He'll be wanting to pat you on the back for sure!\nThank you again, ‹name›. I hope we meet again. You're surely an ally I'm proud to call friend.","rew":"You will learn: Redemption\nExperience: 1,150","done":"You've done well this day, ‹name›. You should take some pride in what you've accomplished.\nEven more so, you should be proud of your abilities. Not everyone can use the power of the Symbol of Life. Calling upon the Light to bring back the dead means you're prepared for one of the ‹class›'s greatest honors: the power of resurrection.\nYou shall have the power to bring back fallen companions much like you did for Henze.\nBe well, ‹name›. The Light shines upon you and you should welcome it wholly.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":45,"n":"Gazin Tenorm","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5628":{"id":5628,"t":"Returning Home","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.","desc":"Ah, yes, hello, ‹name›? I'm glad you stopped to talk for a moment. You are a far way from home at such a young age--I admire such ambition. I wish when I was younger I could have mustered the courage to travel the world.\nThere was a priestess of your order here looking for you not too long ago. She said it was very urgent you returned to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus and speak to Priestess Alathea--it had something to do with your training. I wouldn't dally too long if you can help it.","rew":"You will learn: Starshards\nExperience: 210","done":"Wonderful, you've returned home, ‹name›. It always pleases Tyrande and myself when those we've trained go out into the world and return to us safely. How have things been with you? Does Elune still bless your travels? Perhaps after we speak more about the business at hand, you could tell me more of your travels.\nElwynn Forest Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.3,"y":65.7,"n":"Priestess Josetta","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Priestess Alathea","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8828":{"id":8828,"t":"Winter's Presents","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Great-father Winter. He is located near the Smokywood Pastures vendor area in Orgrimmar.","desc":"I hear Great-father Winter - with the generous support of Smokywood Pastures - has put presents for everyone under the tree in Orgrimmar. I wish I could go, but I've got to look after the PX-238 Winter Wondervolt.\nBut you should definitely check it out. I'm sure Great-father Winter has some presents with your name on them.","rew":"Experience: 10","done":"Oh, ho hello there! You can only be here for one reason: to open your Winter Veil presents.\nNow, don't you worry, Greatfather Winter hasn't forgotten about his favorite ‹race› ‹class›. Look under the tree and you'll find your gifts.\nDuring this season of giving, perhaps your friends would also enjoy receiving some of Smokeywood Pasture's excellent products?\nStormwind City Dun Morogh Stranglethorn Vale Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":67.9,"y":71.4,"n":"Wonderform Operator","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":53.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Wonderform Operator","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.7,"y":73.5,"n":"Wonderform Operator","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.5,"y":69.2,"n":"Great-father Winter","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8508":{"id":8508,"t":"Field Duty Papers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Prepared Field Duty Papers\nProvided: Signed Field Duty Papers","rew":"You will receive:\nSigned Field Duty Papers","back":"I take it you want those papers signed, lad/lass?","done":"Aye, I suppose that little skirmish will pass as field duty nowadays. Take these back to Cenarion Hold, I'm sure they'll have a cushy job ready for you.\nOff you go!\nStart Captain Blackanvil End Captain Blackanvil Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Alliance Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8508\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60.\n1 [ 60 ] Field Duty\nReport for duty at the Ironforge Brigade post near Hive'Zora.\nWindcaller Kaldon Silithus\n2 [ 60 ] Field Duty Papers this quest\nCaptain Blackanvil","cats":["silithus"]},"8348":{"id":8348,"t":"Signet of the Dukes","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 8,800, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Abyssal Signet to Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.\nAbyssal Signet The Duke of Cynders , The Duke of Fathoms , The Duke of Shards , The Duke of Zephyrs","desc":"Huum tells me you've figured out how to summon the Abyssal Dukes! That's quite an accomplishment.\nYou know what else would be quite the accomplishment? Smashing up one of those things really good. That'll cause an impression on their underlings, if you know what I mean. Bring back its signet as proof of the deed.","rew":"You will receive:\nSack of Spoils\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"How did it go with the Abyssal Duke? Did it hit hard?","done":"I knew you were a tough ‹class› the minute I saw you walk into Cenarion Hold. Keep it up!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"428":{"id":428,"t":"Lost Deathstalkers","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Deathstalkers Quinn and Rane Yorick.","desc":"A couple weeks ago two of our Deathstalkers, Rane and Quinn Yorick, were sent on a reconnaissance mission through northern Silverpine. We have not heard from them.\nThey may have become victim to the Scourge, though if that is true then I want it confirmed. Find these Deathstalkers.\nTheir first objective was to scout the farms in northern Silverpine. You should begin your search there.","done":"You found us! And not a moment too soon...","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":40.9,"n":"High Executor Hadrec","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":53.5,"y":13.4,"n":"Rane Yorick","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"79948":{"id":79948,"t":"Defensive magics 101","lv":35,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Defensive Magics 101","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 280","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nDefensive Magics 101 (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1468":{"id":1468,"t":"Children's Week","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Human Orphan Whistle to talk with the child you will be looking after during Children's Week.\nProvided: Human Orphan Whistle","desc":"You're willing to help us here at the orphanage? Bless you, friend; your aid during Children's Week will be invaluable.\nTake this whistle. You will only be able to use it for a short amount of time - typically not longer than Children's Week itself. When you use it, you will be able to talk with the child you've agreed to look after. Using it again will dismiss the child.\nBy all means ‹name› - use the whistle and meet your ward! I'm sure the child will be most eager to meet you.","done":"Um... hi. My name is Randis, and I guess you're looking after me? You're an adventurer, like my mom and dad were. I'm happy to meet you.\nI hope we'll have a lot of fun together. I have some things I'd like to do, and the matron says you'll be like a big brother/sister to me during this week. I'd like that a whole bunch, yes sir/lady.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":56.3,"y":54,"n":"Orphan Matron Nightingale","s":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1068":{"id":1068,"t":"Shredding Machines","lv":23,"min":13,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill the shredders XT:4 and XT:9, then return to Seereth Stonebreak at the border of the Stonetalon Mountains and the Barrens.\nXT:4 slain\nXT:9 slain","desc":"There is a relation to the spiritual magic of shaman and the natural magic of druids. This is why we shaman can hear the plea of the spirits of Stonetalon. Many of their whisperings are lost to me, but one message, one vision, is clear...\nI saw a vision of two man-shaped machines in Windshear Crag, northwest of Greatwood Vale, felling trees with impossible speed. These metal beasts must be stopped!\nIn my vision, the machines were marked with strange symbols:\nXT:4 and XT:9.","rew":"Money: 15 0 gold, 15 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,850\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"The tree spirits wail at the loss of their brethren, ‹name›. You must destroy the shredders XT:4 and XT:9, or I fear Stonetalon will never be healed.","done":"The destruction of the machines XT:4 and XT:9 have soothed many of the spirits of Stonetalon, ‹name›. With their loss, let us hope the Venture Company will remove itself from these mountains.\nFor if they do not, then I fear the atrocities this place has suffered will pale to what lies ahead.\nThe Barrens Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":35.3,"y":27.9,"n":"Seereth Stonebreak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"188":{"id":188,"t":"Tiger Mastery","lv":37,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Ajeck Rouack of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill Sin'Dall and return with her paw.\nPaw of Sin'Dall Sin'Dall","desc":"Here is the final challenge that I will put forth. We've been tracking an elusive tiger for weeks. We call the beast Sin'Dall. See if you can do what no ‹race› has done before: hunt down and kill Sin'Dall. Bring me her paw as proof of your accomplishment.\nTracking her down will be no easy task.","rew":"You will receive:\nTiger Hunter Gloves\nExperience: 2,850","back":"How goes the hunt for Sin'Dall?","done":"Most impressive, I do say! You are a true Master Tiger Hunter, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.6,"y":10.6,"n":"Ajeck Rouack","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"348":{"id":348,"t":"Stranglethorn Fever","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out Witch Doctor Unbagwa and have him summon Mokk the Savage. Bring the Heart of Mokk to Fin Fizracket.\nHeart of Mokk Mokk the Savage","desc":"Sick...so...very s-s-sick....\n...have contracted Stranglethorn Fever...deadly v-v-virus...\n...only cure...is...is...to eat the heart of M-m-m-m-mokk the Savage...elusive white beast...\n...Witch doctor Unbagwa...only one who can s-s-summon....\n...seek Unbagwa in hidden cave on southern cape...\n...hurry...dying...dying....","rew":"You will receive:\nMedicine Blanket\nExperience: 5,850\n+200 reputation with Booty Bay\n-1,000 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"....mother?\n...so cold...\n...heading into the Twisting Nether...h-h-h-hold me mother....","done":"...feel strength returning....\nWhere might be? Booty Bay? Oh my! I had the strangest dream...\n...the weakness has not completely left me....","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.6,"y":76.7,"n":"Fin Fizracket","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"588":{"id":588,"t":"The Fate of Yenniku","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Kin'weelay.","desc":"<Nezzliok speaks.>\nYou have appeased myself and my chief, so I will tell you that which you seek to discover...\nYoung Yenniku is lost to his clan.\nHe was taken by the witchdoctor Zanzil the Outcast. Now Zanzil controls him, body and soul, and only the most potent magic could set him free.\nA magic that you do not have, ‹class›.\nPerhaps your Darkspear allies can offer a hope of Yenniku's salvation. But that, I doubt.","rew":"Experience: 390\n+25 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","done":"Zanzil the Outcast??\nIf Yenniku is held by that troll, a vile and powerful witchdoctor, then I fear that only a faint hope remains. Faint. And tiny as the smallest insect.\nBut still, it is hope.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.2,"y":27.6,"n":"Bubbling Cauldron","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.3,"y":27.7,"n":"Kin'weelay","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"4508":{"id":4508,"t":"Calm Before the Storm","lv":54,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Pestlezugg's Un'Goro Report to Gracina Spiritmight in Darnassus.\nPestlezugg's Un'Goro Report\nProvided: Pestlezugg's Un'Goro Report","desc":"My recent findings and the knowledge we have gained here today needs to reach hands that can quite possibly do something with it. As resourceful as we are here in Gadgetzan, we can't do this alone.\nTake my latest report back to Gracina Spiritmight in Darnassus; she's still at the Temple of the Moon, is she not? She's got friends who are Alliance bigwigs; if we can get them involved in this ‹name›, then we just might make it out of this alive.","rew":"Experience: 550\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","back":"They are fools, ‹name›! They cannot even think to look around them for a greater threat; their irrational hatred of the Horde will be the end of us all. I do not know how much more proof I can give them of the silithid threat short of dropping them in one of the hives so they can see for themselves!\nI'm sorry, you bring news for my attention?","done":"While I genuinely appreciate this, I am not sure what good it will do us. The Alliance ignores threats from any source other than the Horde, and even our own leaders here in Darnassus cannot agree on what exactly this threat is. Fools like Fandral Staghelm theorize that the silithid are nothing like the threat from the ancient past I claim them to be. His ignorance is only surpassed by his arrogance.\nYou have seen the threat yourself, ‹name›. We must remain committed to defeating the silithid!\nTanaris Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.9,"y":27,"n":"Alchemist Pestlezugg","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":41.8,"y":85.6,"n":"Gracina Spiritmight","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2748":{"id":2748,"t":"A Fine Egg","lv":60,"min":42,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fine Egg","rew":"You will receive:\nBox of Spells\n+10 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","back":"A fine egg is one that will, in ideal conditions, hatch free of the evil effects of the Gordunni ogres' incantations.","done":"Very good, ‹name›. I will be sending this egg to Darnassus where I hope it will soon hatch!\nPlease accept this as a symbol of my gratitude.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.4,"y":26.9,"n":"Curgle Cranklehop","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8748":{"id":8748,"t":"The Path of the Protector","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Your continued defense of the children of Kalimdor has been acknowledged. Hand me your signet ring so that I may enhance its powers.","done":"Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, ‹name›. May you never stray from the path of the protector!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2988":{"id":2988,"t":"Witherbark Cages","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Check the cages at the two Witherbark villages, then return to Gryphon Master Talonaxe.\nCheck First Cage\nCheck Second Cage\nCheck Third Cage","desc":"The son of our mightiest gryphon is gone! Swiftwing's heir, Sharpbeak, was lost while hunting with his parents a few days ago, and we believe it was the trolls who took him.\nYou must aid us! Search the cages in the two Witherbark troll villages to see if Sharpbeak is there.","rew":"Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Wildhammer Clan","back":"Have you searched the cages, ‹name›? We must find Sharpbeak!","done":"Sharpbeak wasn't at the villages? Hm... this is grim news. That gryphon is destined to lead the next generation of gryphons. If he is lost then the strength and spirit of our fleet will suffer immensely.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":9.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Gryphon Master Talonaxe","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"1148":{"id":1148,"t":"Parts of the Swarm","lv":35,"min":28,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,750 experience instead of 1,350, 2.04 times as much.","obj":"Bring 1 Silithid Heart, 5 Silithid Talons, and 3 Intact Silithid Carapaces, to Korran at the Crossroads.\nSilithid Heart Silithid Ravager 30 % , Silithid Hive Drone 30 % , Silithid Invader 30 % , Silithid Searcher 30 %\n5 Silithid Talon Silithid Ravager 80 % , Silithid Hive Drone 80 % , Silithid Invader 80 % , Silithid Searcher 80 %\n3 Intact Silithid Carapace Silithid Ravager 80 % , Silithid Hive Drone 80 % , Silithid Invader 80 % , Silithid Searcher 80 %\nProvided: Cracked Silithid Carapace","desc":"You inspect the carapace carefully. As you turn it over in your hands you realize that the chitinous plating is interlaced in such a way that makes it incredibly strong. It's unlike anything you've ever seen. You inspect the rest of the corpse further and realize that these creatures are very powerful and highly evolved.\nLooking down at the carapace again, you think that Korran would enjoy studying more of these creatures. It could help him figure out what these creatures are, and where they come from.","rew":"Experience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Ah, it been a long time since you've come to see me, ‹name›. What can I do for you today? You be looking like you've seen the face of battle recently. Good... good for the Horde and good for you. The more battle you've seen, the more helpful you'll be; stronger, too.","done":"Ahh, you've seen Moktar recently? He always be lookin' out for me. I'm sorry to hear he spends his time watching over his little war band instead of seeing battle, but I'm sure he be takin' great joy in killing members of the Explorers' League.\nYou be smart to bring me these specimens, ‹name›. Along with the eggs we be findin' in the Field of Giants, these should give me a good start in figuring out what these insects are, and what they be wantin'.\nThe Barrens Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.1,"y":29.6,"n":"Korran","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"7628":{"id":7628,"t":"Doomsday Candle","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 35 Black Dragonscales to Gorzeeki Wildeyes in the Burning Steppes.\n35 Black Dragonscale Death Talon Seether 0.8 % in Blackwing Lair , Black Drake 0.7 % , Death Talon Captain 0.4 % in Blackwing Lair , Onyxia's Elite Guard 0.3 % and 4 more","desc":"A Doomsday Candle stores fire and directs it at those who would disrupt your ritual. When creating your Circle of Greater Summoning, if your candle is lit then any wayward demons will be burned by its flames!\nContaining that fire is not easy, and requires the essence within the scales of a black dragon. Acquire those scales from a skinner and bring them to Gorzeeki Wildeyes.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Did you bring the dragonscales, ‹name›? I don't want to start on the candle until I have them... or I might blow up the whole camp!","done":"Ah, very good. I'll need these to contain the fires of the candle. Now that I have the scales, I'll make the candle and hold onto it until you're ready to begin your ritual for the Circle of Greater Summoning.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.7,"y":31.6,"n":"Mor'zul Bloodbringer","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Gorzeeki Wildeyes","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1708":{"id":1708,"t":"Iron Coral","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 loads of Searing Coral to Klockmort Spannerspan in Ironforge.\n20 Searing Coral Iron Coral","desc":"I want to try Furen Longbeard's new techniques on my own piece of armor. And because you helped Furen and he helped me, you're welcome to the armor after I make it!\nTo finish the piece, I need a special coral, searing coral. It grows in only one place--along the coast south of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.\nBring me enough searing coral and I'll get right to work on the armor. And hurry, ‹name›. I'm so eager to get started it's making my toes twist!","rew":"Experience: 1,750","back":"Hello hello, ‹name›! Do you have the searing coral? I can't wait to get to work!","done":"That's the stuff! Well done! Now let me get this smelted and hammered so I can apply Furen's technique with my own and then we can see what happens!\nOh my, oh my! I just know the armor will be very very very tough!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62,"y":28.5,"n":"Klockmort Spannerspan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"7788":{"id":7788,"t":"Vanquish the Invaders!","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Enter Warsong Gulch and defeat the Horde, obtain a Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor, and return to Sentinel Farsong at the Silverwing Grove.\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"Beyond this tunnel you will find a field of strife and turmoil, young ‹class›. The Horde continue to decimate our sacred forest, cutting down the evergreen foliage to power their machines of war.\nEnter Warsong Gulch and defend Silverwing Hold. Push back the invading Horde forces!\nDo this, and earn a talisman of merit. Bring me such a talisman, ‹name›, and I shall reward you.","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\nLevel 25 , requires level 20 Difficulty 20 21 23 28 33 Side Human, Dwarf, Night Elf, Gnome Type PvP Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7788","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"8428":{"id":8428,"t":"Battle of Warsong Gulch","lv":49,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,550\n+100 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","done":"Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"8268":{"id":8268,"t":"Ribbons of Sacrifice","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 39. Gives 650 experience instead of 9,500, 0.07 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Ribbons of Sacrifice to Sentinel Farsong so that the Sentinels may reward you for acting on our behalf.\nWarsong Gulch Ribbon of Sacrifice","desc":"I understand that it can be difficult at times to come out on top in Warsong Gulch. Still, your effort on our behalf - even when victory is not achieved - is important.\nShould you complete one of the trials inside Warsong Gulch and not achieve victory, you will still receive a Ribbons of Sacrifice. Bring it to me so that the Sentinels may reward you for acting on our behalf... even if you weren't able to win this time.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+50 reputation with Warsong Outriders","done":"Well, you did not flee in the face of defeat. You stood your ground, ‹name›, and when it comes right down to it, that is what makes for a true hero. No doubt you will win next time... but nonetheless we thank you for your effort.\nLevel 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Alliance Shareable No Quest ID 8268","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5228":{"id":5228,"t":"The Scourge Cauldrons","lv":53,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.","desc":"Within the lands of former Lordaeron are eight cauldrons - four in the west, and four more entrenched in the east. These cauldrons spew poisons into the air, propagating the plague throughout the land for the Scourge.\nThe necromantic might of Kel'Thuzad is too strong to outright shut down these cauldrons, but we think we might have a way to subvert them to our advantage. My second, Shadow Priestess Vandis, will be your point on this assignment; she'll continue the briefing from here.","rew":"Experience: 525\n+10 reputation with Undercity","done":"From the shadows, brother ‹race›, I bid you greetings. I am to serve as your coordinator for our plan to sabotage the Scourge's cauldrons.\nOur goal will be to change the composition of the plague that the cauldrons create into something that negatively affects the Scourge. In order to affect this change, you will need to secure access to each of the four cauldrons here in the Western Plaguelands.\nThe time has come for you to lead the charge against the Scourge, hero.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.1,"y":68.9,"n":"High Executor Derrington","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83,"y":71.9,"n":"Shadow Priestess Vandis","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"92748":{"id":92748,"t":"Explosive consultation","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Travel to the Dwarven District in Stormwind and find an engineer who can help.","desc":"The supplies you found point to a massive industrial operation somewhere in the Deadmines. There's no question that this is the source of the toxins plaguing the farmland of Westfall. We need to stop it, quickly.\nWhatever's down there will be difficult to destroy. Go to the Dwarven District of Stormwind, and find an engineer who can supply us with some explosives.","rew":"Money: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 575\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Need something blown up?\nWestfall Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":52.4,"y":53,"n":"Alba Fairmoon","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":54.6,"y":8,"n":"Sprite Jumpsprocket","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"6028":{"id":6028,"t":"The Everlook Report","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Everlook Report to Argent Officer Pureheart at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\nEverlook Report\nProvided: Everlook Report","desc":"I am looking for a responsible individual to aid me in a small but nonetheless important matter. I'm here as a representative of the Argent Dawn's interests to the local governance of Everlook. I need to get a progress report to Argent Officer Pureheart at Chillwind Camp; it's a ways from here, located along the southern fringe of the Western Plaguelands.\nIf I may be so bold - this would be a perfect means to introduce yourself to my superior and perhaps earn some work from her!","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn\n+50 reputation with Everlook","back":"Greetings, ‹name›. On behalf of the Argent Dawn, I offer you safety and shelter while you are here at Chillwind Camp. I might also have some work for you...","done":"Very resourceful, Gregor is. He's been dealing with the Steamwheedle Cartel for some time now, and has become an expert on the \"art\" of goblin negotiations. Though it's true that the goblins' primary loyalties lie with those who have the largest coin purses, they also know and respect the value of diplomacy. If anything, it provides them with repeat customers...\nAt any rate, the Argent Dawn acknowledges you for your effort. Please have this, with our thanks.\nWinterspring Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.3,"y":39,"n":"Gregor Greystone","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":83.5,"n":"Argent Officer Pureheart","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5068":{"id":5068,"t":"Breastplate of Bloodthirst","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -50g instead of 0.","obj":"In order to create the Breastplate of Bloodthirst, you will be required to bring the following items back to Malyfous Darkhammer: 1 Pristine Hide of the Beast; 10 Frayed Abomination Stitchings; 5 Arcanite Bars; 5 Skin of Shadow.\nYou will also be required to pay 50 gold pieces for the crafting of the item.\nItem #12731\n10 Frayed Abomination Stitching\n5 Arcanite Bar\n5 Skin of Shadow\nRequired money: 50","desc":"It is said that only one Breastplate of Bloodthirst has ever been created and that it was made for the legendary assassin, Garona. Whether this world will ever see another is doubtful.\nRegardless! Our master crafters can reproduce the item given the necessary components:\n*The pristine hide of the Beast.\n*Frayed abomination stitchings.\n*Arcanite bars.\n*The skin of shadow.\nBEHOLD!","rew":"You will receive:\nBreastplate of Bloodthirst","back":"Unless you've got everything I need, you're wasting my time.","done":"I thought I would be dead and buried before I ever saw this day.\nAn accomplishment of this magnitude can only be overshadowed by the reward.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61,"y":38.8,"n":"Malyfous's Catalogue","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":61,"y":38.8,"n":"Malyfous Darkhammer","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"93948":{"id":93948,"t":"Deliver the signet","lv":9,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the Shadowsong Family Signet to Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.\nProvided: Shadowsong Family Signet","desc":"Since you are going to Valanaar anyway, please deliver the signet ring you recovered from the tower to Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.\nHe will want this back, and more importantly, he will want to learn the fate of his nephew. Talaanis is the High Elder of Zephras Isle and more importantly, he is a good man who is well loved by the people, despite our current hardships. It pains me to think of how he will react to this news. Please express my condolences for his loss.","rew":"Money: 1 50 0 gold, 1 silver, 50 copper Experience: 390\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"What is that you have for me? Oh... oh no.","done":"I... am very sorry to hear that my nephew is dead. I thank you kindly for recovering this, and bringing it to me.\nIt's not common that such capable young shen'dorei come down from the highlands. If you need work, please speak with Valennia Stormfist, the captain of the peacekeepers here in Valanaar. These days we need all the help we can get.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.6,"y":45.4,"n":"Constable Aonda","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Talaanis Shadowsong","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8108":{"id":8108,"t":"Kezan's Taint","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Kezan's Taint","rew":"You will receive:\nKezan's Taint\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"I am ready for you, ‹class›. Once more I will enhance your talisman. I only ask that you continue in your destruction of Hakkar and his minions.\nGive me the talisman.","done":"It is only through our combined efforts that we will stop the Soulflayer.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]},"8188":{"id":8188,"t":"Vodouisant's Vigilant Embrace","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring me thise things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!\nPrimal Hakkari Idol\nPunctured Voodoo Doll\nPrimal Hakkari Idol Jin'do the Hexxer in Zul'Gurub , Bloodlord Mandokir in Zul'Gurub\nPunctured Voodoo Doll Voodoo Slave 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadowcaster 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Gurubashi Axe Thrower 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Gurubashi Blood Drinker 0 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more","desc":"Zanza can create the ancient troll enchantments with the right components. The first is a primal Hakkari idol that must be taken from the most powerful of the Hakkari lieutenants: Jin'do and the Bloodlord.\nThe second is a punctured voodoo doll. These can be found in the piles of refuse that litter this foul place. Look inside the jinxed hoodoo.\nBring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","rew":"You will receive:\nVodouisant's Vigilant Embrace\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Bring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","done":"Use it well, ‹class›. Show the Hakkari no mercy!\nStart Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub End Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Horde Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8188","cats":["zulgurub"]}});